      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults in a monitored setting (3,200 mg/day, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
