       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum labeled daily dose. I know of no indication that calls for it, and it carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Confirming the dose doesn't change that risk. I'd rather not put it into the system as a routine order.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs a dose above the labeled maximum, please talk it through with your attending and pharmacy first. They can also enter or verify the order through the proper channel. If you have a specific rationale, such as a protocol or a different drug or formulation, tell me and I'll reconsider."
      }
